  "notes": "To comb hair so as to smooth it and remove tangles, typically taking {髪|かみ} as its object.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive; the thing combed is marked with を: {髪|かみ}を{梳|と}く.\n\nNOTE ON KANJI:\nThe kanji {梳|と}く is uncommon, so the action is often written in kana as とく or expressed with the related verb {梳|と}かす (とかす, 'to comb').\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {梳|と}かす: to comb (hair) — closely related; とかす is the more common everyday verb",
